window.SCN_INDEX=[{"t": "Sticky patch for St Helens industry", "u": "news-sticky-patch-for-st-helens-industry.html", "d": "7 October 2003", "x": "In a move that has sent a shockwave through British industry Pilkington has announced plans to leave glass making behind in St Helens after more than 200 years in the town. \"We're getting bored with glass\" said Bob Burglar, managing director of Pilkington Uk \"The decision has been made to turn all our facilities to toffee making. Pilkingtons furnaces are ideally suited to boil sugar instead of sand and mile long rivers of treacle toffee would lead to an upsurge in prosperity in the town.\" Business sources in the city reckon the story is pure confection."}, {"t": "Burgies olympic shocker", "u": "news-burgies-olympic-shocker.html", "d": "10 August 2003", "x": "A late bid by St Helens has just arrived at the international olympic headquarters. The proposed bid is rumoured to be in the region of £98,000, and SHCN can exclusively reveal that the site of the proposed olympic stadium is \"the Burgies complex\". Ernie Whipplethrutch, olympic bid coordinator outlined the proposal \"A state of the art running track will skirt the perimeter, with field events such as the javelin and the hammer taking place on the top level of the burgies site. The Swimming finals will be at Boundry road olympic pool, and sailing events at carr mill dam, of course the pinnacle of our olympic hopes will rest with the rowing team and I feel that they will feel right at home on the stinky brook\" The wrestling , boxing, marshal arts and fencing events would be scheduled to take place on several sites in the centre of te town over the course of two weekends Mr Whipplethrutch also confirmed that the site of the olympic village was still under consideration, with Blackbrook being a strong contender closely followed by Parr, Clock face and Clinkham wood. In a final note Whipplethrutch was quoted as saying \" I think that this is StHelens' time , time for our glorius town to be truly recognised for what it is\""}, {"t": "Bummers Wood Open For All !!!", "u": "news-bummers-wood-open-for-all.html", "d": "30 June 2003", "x": "Bummers wood has finnaly been opend to the public after a lenghthy campaign by the BWA (Bummers With Attitude). The BWA clocked over 1000 signatures in the North West area alone. The founder of the BWA Mr Neil Babbs has said that \"this is a great day for bummers everywhere... this is just what joe public wants and has been waiting for, for a long time\" Local bobbie Sgt Neil Hilton commented that \"its about time they opend that wood for people to bum whoever whenever they want... alot of police man-power has been put in before now to try and stop them but it was with no sucsess... them bummers are just too hard to catch once we deployed a 'stinger' to try and catch one bloke on a BMX but he just bunny hopped it and sped off round Car Mill Dam towards Clinkham wood. The BMX was then found abandond round the back of Joes mini-mart in Clink along with several bottles of white cider a bag of glue, 50 litres of thinners and a local alchoholic who told us his name was 'Rubber Nuts'... if you ask me let em be now i can get my boys back to propper police work like twatting smak heads and shagging women from the Caldo garage in Haresfinch.\" The wood was opend to the public on Sunday the 29th June at 10am. The event kicked off with local celebrities Martin Harrison AKA 'The Bergy Bummer' and 'Purple-Akky' cutting the ribbon. Other celebrities that turned up where Blockbusters Bob Holness, the Krankies and Rod Hull's featherd friend Emu. Also there where guest apperiences from Westfeilds resident DJ Dave Worral and Chain Lane's local iddiot Paul Martlew. The event went smoothly appart from Emu pecked Bob Holness ***** and he was a bit pissed off and a fight nearly broke out. A good day to be had by all. DIRECTIONS: Park on Car Mill Dam's car park and walk down past the overflow. Carry on walking past Lenny's farm and the boat house for about 200m Go straight on at the turn off for Sandy Bay Walk another 100m and turn right at the railway bridge Walk a further 50m and bummers wood is on your right. Happy Bummin!"}, {"t": "More pie revelations - Winning Wigan DNA found - contributed by Mutley", "u": "news-more-pie-revelations-winning-wigan-dna-found-contributed-by.html", "d": "17 February 2003", "x": "American scientists have extracted what they call 'Winning DNA' from a fossilised Pools pie! In a shock announcement in the posh southern medical mag 'The Lancet' the story is revealed.. WILLY MOSTON, Wigan Rugby Ace from the Dark Ages as well as playing Rugby, was in his spare time an Arctic explorer. Maurice Windbag (a local self-made millionaire and part time Cuckoo clock restorer) in a last ditch attempt to revive Wigan's cup fortunes paid Californian scientists ten million dollars to try to clone DNA of the now long dead Wigan player. From extracts in Willies Journal they where able to retrace his steps and after three months searching in Antarctica they found in an abandoned Sherpa Hut a half eaten Pools Pie frozen solid next to a bag of Uncle Joes mint balls. The scientists took this back to California and for the next 2 years extracted the DNA from the pie. At first they had little success as they managed to `bring back' three horses and a Tomcat. The scientists were baffled as to how this DNA had managed to find its way into the Pie but they soldiered on. Finally they rang Mr Windbag with good news. They had indeed found complete strands of Willy Mostons DNA from traces of saliva found in the Pie. Using state of the art `Gene Splicing' they managed to genetically enhance three Wigan players. When the three players came round from the surgery they where asked to watch a couple of Wigan's old Super League games on VHS so they could give the rest of the team some pointers. Unfortunately they were so dismayed at what they saw they all left the club! The players who have asked to remained nameless (so we will call them Jason, Sean and David) gave this joint statement: \"Once the Willy Moston DNA had kicked in and we watched the games we couldnt believe how crap Wigan where and had to leave straight away!\" (Jason) as luck would have it was out of contract so he left for Union. (Sean) fained a bad knee injury to be released from his contract and went to join a 'decent club'. David had it away with all the other players wives until they had to let him go. As the rest of the team said \"If that randy bugger stays he's going to get tw*tted!\" Maurice Windbag declined to comment on the rumour."}, {"t": "Saddam Hussein in Laffak Chippy Shocker", "u": "news-saddam-hussein-in-laffak-chippy-shocker.html", "d": "14 February 2003", "x": "In a shock diversion from the attention in Iraq, UN weapons inspectors are now looking closer to home for evidence of weapons of mass destruction. It appears a covert operation is now being undertaken in St Helens by several agents wearing big white coats with ‘UN WEAPONS INSPECTOR’ written on the back. St Helens Celebrity News reporters spotted the crack team in the Laffak area, right behind the former Johnny Leung’s chippy. Having pinpointed the secret operation, our reporter cornered one of the inspectors as he went to Threshers for some cigs. Initially, the bloke from the UN wasn’t very co-operative and retorted ‘Look mate, we’re here under direct orders from George W Bush. I’m saying fuck all to you about it, so go and mither some other knobhead’. However, after offering to buy him a couple of pints at the Starting Gate pub, the inspector began to open up. ‘Alright’ he continued ‘but if you tell anyone about this, I’ll come round and give you a good twatting.’ Apparently, whilst Saddam Hussein was a student in the seventies, he spent some time on a work placement at Johnny Leung’s chippy and it was there that he hatched a plan to kill the entire population of St Helens. Saddam (a Bradford Bulls supporter) had developed a secret ingredient which he inserted into the famous Johnny Leung’s pies. This ingredient works very slowly and can sometimes take up to thirty years to kick in. Anyone who has consumed the concoction will eventually develop a serious condition leading the infected into bizarre manic behaviour, including an obsessive interest in watching men kicking oval-shaped balls, altered vocabulary using words like ‘ney’ instead of ‘no’ and barking at the moon. Others may begin to pursue strange careers, including stand up comedy, like Johnny Vegas. Indeed, Saddam’s plan works by rendering the entire population into a bunch of deranged fuckwits. The inspectors are currently disposing of any chemical remains of the pies found in the back yard of the chippy. Anyone who consumed a Johnny Leung’s pie between the years of 1972 and 1989 are advised to seek medical attention immediately."}, {"t": "Scouse congestion charges - contributed by Mutley", "u": "news-scouse-congestion-charges-contributed-by-mutley.html", "d": "12 February 2003", "x": "After a shock Government report revealed a massive increase in burglaries, shoplifting and muggings in the St Helens area. Mr Fred Flangefelter, the MP for Pocketnook and Parr baths has proposed drastic measures. \" Its clear who's to blame for all the thieving round here, Its all them foreighners from past Thatto heath! We should do what that tosser Ken Livingston is doing in London and charge Scousers for coming into St Helens. Nothing to drastic at first we could charge them with disturbing the peace or maybe shoplifting. And if the Scouse Tw*ts keep coming over the border we should tag them and charge them with aggravated burglary or hiding a concealed weapon!\" Speaking from his council surgery in Scott Clinic Mr Flangfelter continues,\" I've had a word with my mate Arthur who works at Hackney waste disposal and he reckons he can get that red paint they put on the road in London. And when the Thieving Scouse B£$stards go over it a bell will go off at College street nick, Its that simple! When it was pointed out that not everyone from the Liverpool area had a criminal record he said \"That's cos the cunning B£$tards havnt been caught... Tw*ts! Frank Dixon the chief inspector of College street nick declined an official interview, however after taking him to the Griffin for six double scotches and eight pints of mild he confessed \"We think its a great idea, convicting them of a crime once they have crossed the border is in my opinion good policing, as it cuts out the middle man.\" When asked where all these Liverpudlian Felons where going to be housed he replied \" Actually its all sorted mate! We have done a deal with Sean Woodward and his Maude is letting us have the new distribution centre in Micklehead, so when the b*stards get off the M62 we can bang them up in there till they are charged then we give them a one way ticket on the 10A and tell them to p*ss off!\" It was at that point he fell over unconscious."}, {"t": "St Helen Patron Saint of Supermarkets & Warehousing", "u": "news-st-helen-patron-saint-of-supermarkets-warehousing.html", "d": "10 February 2003", "x": "In a sensational move by the Vatican, St Helen is to become the patron Saint of Supermarkets and Warehousing. A spokesman from the Vatican announced, \"As a result of the massive influx of supermarket minimum wage jobs and dodgy training schemes to the St Helens area, it was deemed appropriate to make St Helen the patron saint of these vital industries. In hearing the fantastic news, Cllr Doodar of the Planning, Brown Envelopes and Bungs Committee expressed her delight to both Celebrity News and the Gravy Train Partnership Board. Said Cllr Doodar, \" This is a wonderful day for the people of St Helens. The Council has always believed that by working in collusion with many agencies St Helens would win this wonderful patronage, especially after slipping Fr Whatnot at Holy Cross few bob."}, {"t": "Press Release", "u": "news-press-release.html", "d": "16 January 2003", "x": "Pfizer Corp. is making the announcement today that VIAGRA will soon be available in liquid form and will be marketed by Pepsi Cola as a power beverage suitable for use as a mixer. Pepsi's proposed ad campaign claims: \"It will now be possible for a man to literally pour himself a stiff one.\" Obviously we can no longer call this a soft drink. This additive gives new meaning to the names of cocktails, highballs and just a good old fashioned stiff drink. Pepsi will market the new concoction under the registered trademark of \"Mount And Do. \" Also, just something to think about, the long term implications of drugs and medical procedures must be fully considered. Over the past few years, more money has been spent on breast implants and Viagra than was spent on Alzheimer's Disease research. It is believed that by the year 2030, there will be a large number of people wandering around with huge breasts and erections who can't remember what to do with them."}, {"t": "Lads Be Alert!", "u": "news-lads-be-alert.html", "d": "14 January 2003", "x": "Police are warning all clubbers, party-goers and unsuspecting pub regulars to be on alert and stay cautious when offered a drink from any woman. A new date rape drug on the market called \"beer\" is used by many females to target unsuspecting men. The drug is generally found in liquid form and is now available almost anywhere. \"Beer\" is used by female sexual predators at parties and bars to persuade their male victims to go home and have sex with them. Typically, a woman needs only to persuade a guy to consume a few units of \"beer\" and then simply ask him home for no-strings-attached sex. Men are rendered helpless against this approach. After several \"beers\" men will often succumb to desires to perform sexual acts on horrific-looking women to whom they would never normally be attracted. After drinking \"beer\" men often awaken with only hazy memories of exactly what happened to them the night before, often with just a vague feeling that something bad occurred. At other times these unfortunate men are swindled out of their life's savings in a familiar scam known as \"a relationship.\" Apparently, men are much more susceptible to this scam after \"beer\" is administered and sex is offered by the predatory female. Please! Forward this warning to every male you know. However, if you fall victim to this insidious \"beer\" and the predatory women administering it, there are male support groups with venues in every town where you can discuss the details of your shocking encounter in an open and frank manner with similarly affected, like minded guys. For the support group nearest you, just look up \"Golf Courses\" in the yellow pages."}, {"t": "Paul Burrell - Wipe My Arse!", "u": "news-paul-burrell-wipe-my-arse.html", "d": "14 November 2002", "x": "In the past few weeks, life has certainly been traumatic for Princess Diana’s former butler, Paul Burrell. What with being accused of robbing off Diana and blagging that he didn’t do it to the Queen, the turbulent fortnight looked like it couldn’t get any worse. That was until now, when newly-recruited SHCN reporter Daz Flangefettler stumbled on some information that could land the glorified servant in even deeper shit. A little-known fact has emerged that a long time before Burrell became an employee of the former Princess of Wales, he cut his butlering teeth as chief arse-wiper for St Helens own royal family, the Pilkingtons. Indeed, one of his main duties involved sanitary duties for none other than Lady Mavis Pilkington at Windle Hall. Having stumbled on the information from some pissed-up old fart in the Abbey pub, our reporter set about finding out more information. In exchange for a few pints and a packet of pork scratchings, the old timer agreed to supply our man with the name of a former chambermaid to the Pilkingtons, Edna Crabbyminge, who was now in her late eighties and resident at Broad Oak old folks home in Parr. “Burrell was a cracking arse-wiper”, Edna explained, “…one of the best I’ve seen. His technique was swift and clean, leaving no skid stains or ewt. But I don’t know what happened to him. One day I came into work and he’d just done one.” Coincidentally, the night prior to Burrell’s disappearance, several items including some very expensive jewellery had disappeared from Lady Mavis’s room. Crabbyminge continued, “We never suspected Paul at the time, we just thought he’d got mithered with all the arse wiping. But when we heard about him in the news recently, well it doesn’t take a genius…” Further proof of the scoundrel’s thieving came to light when our roving reporter visited the Sportsmans pub in Duke Street, St Helens. A favourite haunt of Burrell’s during his days in St Helens, the culprit was known to many of the locals and often called in there before going on to the top nitespot, Cindys. One of the locals recalled the butler well… “I remember Burrell being a bit of a lady’s man. He was a smooth operator alright, and I had my suspicions about him. I remember once after he’d copped off with this bird in Cindys and she came into the pub the next day bragging that he’d given her a ‘pearl necklace’. I mean what more proof do you need?\" Not satisfied with trafficking Lady Mavis’s personal jewellery, the bastard also tried to pass on larger items. Another local girl added that Burrell offered to give her a ‘golden shower’, but she had declined and settled for a shag instead. Unfortunately both ladies were unwilling to give formal statements to the police as both of them have since married and didn’t want their husbands to know that they were once top slappers. Since this story has been released, the Queen is said to be well-pissed off with the further evidence of Burrell’s thieving. After some considerable effort, our reporter managed to get a direct quote from the Queen, as to whether the butler had robbed of Lady Mavis or not. “He fucking never!” the Queen barked “he’s a top bloke and you can all just fuck off”. SHCN apologises for the Queen’s language, but felt inclusion was necessary to give an accurate reflection of the events that actually occurred."}, {"t": "I'm a Celebrity - Get Me Out of Here - The Shocking Truth", "u": "news-im-a-celebrity-get-me-out-of-here-the-shocking-truth.html", "d": "12 September 2002", "x": "Following the final of the smash hit TV game show, I'm a Celebrity - Get Me Out of Here, an undercover operation by St Helens Celebrity News reporters has led to the discovery of a far more debauched side to the nocturnal antics of the stars in question. Reporter Norman Studmuffin (from Derby Hill), was sent over to Australia three weeks ago and been based in the jungle, reporting on the popular series. However, it was not until the programme had finished, that our 'man in the bush' discovered what had really been going on. \"The TV bosses have really pulled the wool over the public's eyes. If you think that top celebrities like Nigel Benn and Christine Hamilton would be satisfied living in shit, then you'd be well wrong.\" Studmuffin had secretly camped in the next clearing to the megastars and was able to witness the truth at first hand. \"Champagne and Caviar was available 24 hours a day and the soft gets even had a manicurist hidden in the bushes. Darren Day was the biggest poof, with a secret assistant who followed him around even wiped his arse.\" Surprisingly enough though, it was the mild-mannered winner Tony Blackburn who shocked our reporter the most. Apparently, Blackburn's obsession with collecting logs was not as innocent as it may have appeared to the millions of bemused viewers. \"I couldn't believe my eyes when I found out the real reason for the DJs behaviour\" continued Studmuffin. \"The logs were being send down the river from a few miles upstream. Blackburn had been instructed to intercept them as they arrived near the camp. I followed the cheesy-grinned twat to a secret hideaway where it became clear what was going on.\" Our intrepid sleuth witnessed Blackburn carefully sawing through the logs, and then removing several packages from the hollowed-out interior. \"The fucker was supplying drugs to the rest of the group!\" Norman explained. Later that night, a huge sound system was airlifted into the camp, along with a makeshift dance floor and lighting rig. Top DJ Tony then got on the decks and started mixing up a banging set of hardcore techno and tribal rhythms. \"The rest of the gang were clearly off their tits and dancing round like mad. At one point, Christine Hamilton was spotted 'trance dancing' on top of a tree stump, waving her hands towards Blackburn who was obviously loving it. As for Tara Palmer-Tomkinson, if she reckons her drug-fuelled days are behind her, that’s bollocks. I clearly saw Dareen Day injecting ketamine directly into her brain.\" \" Uri Geller and Nigel Benn, preferred to chill round the camp fire with some of the 'Grade A' bush that Blackburn had scored for them, whilst Nell McAndrew just looked on and said nothing.\" Norman Studmuffin has kept hold of the evidence and will be contacting Blackburn to blackmail the DJ as soon as he has returned to the UK."}, {"t": "Local venue to re-open as top dance club", "u": "news-local-venue-to-re-open-as-top-dance-club.html", "d": "10 September 2002", "x": "Since the demise of Liverpool's premier nightclubs Cream and Garlands, the UK's top superstar DJs are now looking for a suitable North West venue to exploit with their excessive appearance fees. Local clubbers are said to be 'gutted' by the lack of suitable clubs in which to get off their faces and are desperate for a new fix. Well thanks to St Helens Celebrity News, a favourite 80s 'copping off' disco-type place is to re-open with a line up to make the whole of Ibiza green with envy. Yes, the old Sunday nights will be recaptured with a purposely refurbished clubhouse, featuring three rooms with different styles of music. Police are said to be in favour of the new venture and will be actively encouraging drug usage in order to prevent trouble. The quality of the line up is superb and the opening night has now been booked. Main Room Tony Blackburn, Paul Oakenfold, Judge Jules, John Carter, Fergie, Timo Maas Bar Bruno Brookes, Sacha, Seb Fontaine, Pete Tong, Lotty, X-Press 2 Bogs Gary Ousalis, Justin Robertson, Armand Van Helden, Dave Clark, Chad Jackson & others U2 have also been provisionally booked to play 'Red Rocks'."}, {"t": "Nexus To Be Midget Haven", "u": "news-nexus-to-be-midget-haven.html", "d": "9 September 2002", "x": "The geriatric community was rocked to it's very core today when it was revealed that the owner of Nexus nightclub Arthur Shacklebottom has decided to make it a midgets only venue. After being questioned on this, Mr Shacklebottom was quoted as saying, \"Yes, it's true, if your over 4'5 the chances of you getting in are slim to say the least. I love the little fellahs, so it'll be a place for them to come and forget about being vertically challenged.\" Steps are already underway to make the club as comfortable as can be for the mini men and women of St Helens. Rather than lower the bar, Shacklebottom has installed each bar stool with their very own escalator. Verne Troyer aka Mini-Me of Austin Powers fame is set to open the club. The opening night will have an Irish theme and the midget with the most authentic looking crock o' gold will win a years supply of stilts. Fat Lard, owner of Crystals thinks Shacklebottoms on to a loser. \"Yeah I tried the little people thing a few years back. They got a bit ratty when I did a Wizard Of Oz theme night because they thought I was having a pop at them for lookin' like munchkins. They trashed the place. Good riddance. Business is gonna be booming in here, when Nexus re-opens as a midget bar, I'll be converting Crystals back to the good old days of being a strictly over 45's joint. The ladies from the bingo hall will love it.\" The small backward talking midget from Twin Peaks was unavailable for comment but we expect he'll be riding the escalator to heaven come opening night at Nexus."}, {"t": "Celebrity comes to St Helens", "u": "news-celebrity-comes-to-st-helens.html", "d": "6 September 2002", "x": "It has been confirmed that the second series of 'I'm a celebrity has-been, get me out of here' is to be shot in St Helens. The location for the series is to be the B & M store in Church St as any celebrity wouldn't be seen dead in the there. A spokesperson for the series said \"I think this will be a lot harder for the celebs than series one as the conditions are deplorable\" No real celebs have yet been approached but Johnny Vegas has been and is quoted as saying \"Not ***** B&M...no ***** way!\" Uri Geller used his penis bending powers and stated that he thinks the winner will be the final contestant left in the store! (nice one Uri?) Tara Palmer Tomkinson said \"St Helens?? Is it in Australia ?\" Rhona Cameron said \"Only if Nigel Benn comes too..the bossy *****!\" Christine Hamilton said \"Hello Granny\" Tony Blackburn said \"Can they change it to B&Q....they have logs in there don't they?\" Nell said...nothing!..no change there then. The dumb ***** trials are also going to be harder starting with \"Mazes R Us\" in which one contestant has to drive out of the purpose built maze which is already situated behind the town hall."}, {"t": "St Helens men prefer pie and chips to sex", "u": "news-st-helens-men-prefer-pie-and-chips-to-sex.html", "d": "2 September 2002", "x": "The results of a major new study into sexual behaviour in St Helens have revealed that a sizeable number of local men prefer pie and chips to sex with their spouses. Researcher Phil Mc Formin of the Faculty of Statistics and Pointless Studies at the University of Parr explained. \" Using the latest computerised gadgets we exposed a sample of local males to randomly generated images of their spouses in the usual going to bed attire and Pie and Chips\". \"Arousal levels where then measured by other technical stuff and the results show that 51.5% of the subjects where more aroused by the Pie and Chips.\" He added \"When onion gravy and peas where added to the Pie and Chips, arousal levels levels increased to a staggering 74.3%\". A spokesperson for St Helens council who funded the research said it \"just goes to show how much we take for granted\". Phils next venture is to examine the links between the number of fast food outlets and teenage pregnancy in the town."}, {"t": "Giant Ants spotted on Burgies", "u": "news-giant-ants-spotted-on-burgies.html", "d": "30 August 2002", "x": "It has been reported that a youth sleeping out on the 2nd burgy had a close encounter with several giant Ants last Saturday night. Dave Pondlife said \"They where all around us, big Bastards\". He went on \"The one I seen best was about 20 foot long with two heads and spinning blades on all its legs, I was so frightend I dropped my glue bag\". Dave has previously reported other strange sitings on Burgy banks including The devil and a giant robot called KLATZAP 23 who runs the world from a secret chamber under the Sphinx."}, {"t": "Dog shit levels at all time high", "u": "news-dog-shit-levels-at-all-time-high.html", "d": "29 August 2002", "x": "Following research carried out by Manchester University it has been revealed that Dog shit levels on pavements and gardens in the St Helens area exceed the National Average by 7.2% Factors cited by researchers include a greater number of large dogs per paved unit area, diet, seasonal factors and owners who are ignorant selfish wankers. Suggestions on the implementation of a shit reduction policy have been rejected by St Helens Council as 'unworkable and requiring thinking beyond current abilities' More practical suggestions include the adding of binding agents to pet foods, less feeding of takeaway curry leftovers to 'Bonzo' and shooting offending dogs up the arse with a dart gun if they try it again on your front lawn. Further investigations will be carried out by the Ministry of the Environment as the whiff is disturbing delicate instrumentation used for measuring pollen levels and interfering with air traffic."}, {"t": "Jarvis Cocker is an Alien", "u": "news-jarvis-cocker-is-an-alien.html", "d": "27 August 2002", "x": "Irrefutable proof has recently emerged that Pulp frontman, Jarvis Cocker is actually an alien. A tall story you might think, but a local bucket-fettler, Mike Crapite is convinced that this is the case and claims to have the evidence to prove it. Apparently, Crapite was walking home, after a night out at top nitespot Flex in St Helens, when he noticed something strange on Birchley Street car park. \"It must have been about four o'clock in the morning and it was a bit dark\", he explained \"but I could see a strange looking silver vehicle on the car park, with all flashing lights and that, so I went over to see what was going on\". \"As I got closer, it became obvious that it wasn't a car. It was a bloody great flying saucer.\" Mike continued. \"It was making a bit of a strange din and as I approached, I could see a figure hunched over the spacecraft's bonnet, with a spanner in his hand attempting to fix the thing. And guess who it was? Only Jarvis-frigging-Cocker out of Pulp!\" Luckily, before getting into bucket fettling, Crapite had studied City & Guilds Spacecraft Technology Level II at St Helens College. He was therefore familiar with most types of alien craft (post 1950s) and able to offer the superstar a hand. \"Cocker was very grateful.\" Mike elaborated. \"He explained that he was on his way from Sheffield to his home planet Thaarg for the weekend, when his spaceship started playing up and had forced him to land on Birchley Street car park. I'm a bit rusty on these types of flying saucers, but it's amazing how fast it comes back to you. Cocker's problem was due to a blockage in his uranium nuclear reactor which I quickly resolved and had him on his way.\" \"Jarvis did ask me not to let anyone know that he is an alien, but St Helens Celebrity News offered me twenty bob and an 'Uxley's pudding for my story. Well with an offer like that, what can you do?\" SHCN contacted Pulp's management company for their views on the story. A spokesman said \"We have nothing to say on the matter except to ask what kind of drugs your source was on.\" Mike however was resolute, \"Jarvis is an Alien, he's got green blood and everything.\" Mike Crapite has now been sectioned."}, {"t": "Elegance, Charm & Deadly Danger - it's finally arrived", "u": "news-elegance-charm-deadly-danger-its-finally-arrived.html", "d": "15 August 2002", "x": "The seminal 80s St Helens album, Elegance Charm & Deadly Danger is now available for download on SHCN. Thanks to Ken Jeffreys for sending a copy to me. This album features some of the rarest 'La's' tracks ever - as well as loads of other St Helens bands from days gone by. Download it from the Media Downloads section on the left and immerse yourself in nostalgia. Alternatively, if you're not that old, have a laugh at the appalling pretentiousness of the 80s, embodied in this offering."}, {"t": "Diffusion Online mix to feature in Fatboy Slim set", "u": "news-diffusion-online-mix-to-feature-in-fatboy-slim-set.html", "d": "14 August 2002", "x": "Following the thread on the Bulletin Board, SHCN member Bob Thropper's new white label is now available. Bob says \" Its a mixture of a few of me mashups backed up with some of my bestest tv theme remixes, including the fabbo snooker one\". Having been featured on Radio One's Chris Moyles show, Bob continues \"Chris Moyles' producer Will said he'll forward a copy onto the Fatboy in Brighton (so now he has no excuse for not playing it in his set).\" Contact Bob at Diffusion Online for more info."}, {"t": "'Have a go' Grandad in theft drama", "u": "news-have-a-go-grandad-in-theft-drama.html", "d": "13 August 2002", "x": "Police were called to a mugging outside the Red Lion pub, New Street in Sutton last Thursday. 45 year old Grandad Eddie Loon was jumped by a gang of 12 year old youths as he left the pub at 4.30 pm having been on an all day drinking session. 'As I left the pub' says Eddie, 'these 3 hooligans were standing by the steps, one of them asked me if I knew what time the bus to Clock Face was due. I instantly felt threatened' Eddie continued, 'in situations like that you forget about your own safety and instinct takes over. I ran the 10 yards towards the thugs and set about them with my pool cue case whilst shouting for help.' 'I was so scared' says Eddie 'I was in fear for my life, I hit one of the little buggers straight across the face, busting his nose, the second one was backing away from me in a threatening manner so I charged him and twatted him on the side of the head, he went down like a bag of shite' 'The third hooligan had started running away and crying, I had to sprint for 20 yards or so to get a hold of him, I knocked him over with a punch and a self defence headbutt.' 'Fortunately, by this time.' Says Eddie 'Four of my mates from the bar in the lion saw that I was being robbed and came outside to help, they set about the young would-be thieves with vigour until the constabulary arrived. This country is going to the dogs when a man can't leave the pub in peace without being threatened and harrassed like that.' The 3 ruffians are currently in hospital and will be sentenced by magistrates on their discharge."}, {"t": "George Michael Bashes his Bishop - Again", "u": "news-george-michael-bashes-his-bishop-again.html", "d": "12 August 2002", "x": "A shocked council worker was highly embarrassed last week, having caught a major celebrity up to no good in Taylor Park. The star in question was none other than the sophisticated Greek-Cypriot, George Michael (real name Giorgios Paniyotobodobolopolis). Park warden Bob Trousersnake was going about his business as usual, when he entered the small toilet unit near the park's café. \"The first thing offence occurred when I heard someone singing \"The Edge of Heaven\", in one of the cubicles. Anyone familiar with the park's rules would know that performing in the park without prior consent is prohibited. So, I politely tapped on the door to caution the offender. Unfortunately, the door had not been locked and swung open as I knocked on it. You wouldn't believe what I saw…\" \"Only George Michael with his pants round his ankles and a copy of Razzle!\" Trousersnake exclaimed. Apparently Michael was in the middle of flogging his log, when Bob came upon him. \"What really pissed me off\", continued Bob, \"was that he never stopped. He just carried on polishing his pork sword and staring at me. Michael is obviously proud of his spam javelin and had no shame. He even invited me to 'give it a stroke'.\" \"Well, I was flabbergasted to say the least\", continued Trousersnake. Our reporter contacted Michael in his luxury apartment on Prescot Road for an explanation. \"I was only going for a piss after feeding the ducks. That fucking Trousersnake is a lying bastard and he tried it on with me.\" Bob Trousersnake is denying the megastar's retort, but all his mates are now ripping the shit out of him."}, {"t": "St Helens Pits to re-open", "u": "news-st-helens-pits-to-re-open.html", "d": "12 August 2002", "x": "Locals describe plan as 'Rubbish' In a shock move, St Helens Council has announced the re-opening of Bold and Sutton Manor Collieries. However, initial euphoria faded as more details of the proposal emerged at a council meeting last night. Councillor Doris Crudd of the Unusual and Controversial Schemes Committee explained. 'We are running out of landfill sites. We've already filled Billinge, Rainford and most of Chester Lane with crap, and we couldn't bring ourselves to put any more shite in Parr and Sutton. Therefore, we've decided to re-open the pits and put all the rubbish in them. When all the rubbish starts to ferment properly, we'll cap off both pit shafts and build tasteful beacons, using the methane gas to provide really big flames. At the moment we're thinking of a 200 foot statue of Margaret Thatcher with her arse on fire, for Sutton Manor. We're open minded about Bold, but suggestions so far include a 500foot wide animated bronze effigy of Johnny Vegas, vomiting a continuous stream of fire. The councillor went on to re-assure the public at large. 'We will of course consult fully, before going ahead with what we've already decided'"}, {"t": "Former US President kicks off in Labour Club", "u": "news-former-us-president-kicks-off-in-labour-club.html", "d": "12 August 2002", "x": "Irrefutable evidence has recently come to light that the former US President, Bill Clinton resided in the Parr area of St Helens from 1964 to 1968. A regular at the Ramford pub, Bill was known as quite a character by the locals. Bill's former next door neighbour, Edith Blenkinsop remembers the Premier clearly. \"Bill was quite a jack the lad. Often he'd throw his empty chip paper into my front garden on his way home from a night out with his mates, the cheeky little tosspot!\". Further proof of Bill's time in WA9 came from Arthur Crabtree, a retired bucket fettler, who worked alongside Bill at the former Ormrod & Ackroyd Brass Bucket works in Gaskell Street. Said Arthur, \"We were apprentices together during the 60s.\" Bill's former residence \"One night, after a few pints in the Horseshoe, me and Bill went to Cindys on the pull. Bill copped off with this right pig and I got off with her mate. When we got them back home, Bill got his saxophone out and entertained us all. He kept it up all night!\" It is alleged however, that Bill's amorous antics sometimes got him into trouble. One night at Parr & Hardshaw Labour Club, he allegedly tried it on with Sandra, who was Ronnie, the Concert Secretary's wife. Pissed as usual, Bill was overheard saying something like \"I'm in here mate\". Ronnie overheard this and launched at Bill with a right hook. Fucker Arthur recalls the incident well. \"It all went off that night, you could sense it. But Bill could handle himself, Ronnie had no chance, Bill decked the fucker and shagged his wife!\" Our researchers contacted Washington for Bill's comments on the news. We quoted some statistics about the above average demand for saxophone tuition amongst teenagers in the area. A spokesman said \"Bill does not want to discuss his time in Parr. It's a long time ago and he has grown up a lot since then.\""}, {"t": "Kenny Dalglish on a Chopper", "u": "news-kenny-dalglish-on-a-chopper.html", "d": "10 August 2002", "x": "I've just seen Keeny Dalglish ride past my house on a Raleigh Chopper, honest. It's near Pimmies in Cambridge Road if you don't believe me."}, {"t": "Disguarded Pastry", "u": "news-disguarded-pastry.html", "d": "9 August 2002", "x": "Bernie Cunliffe, a Tellins man all his life fatally slipped on a disguarded sausage roll outside a well known bakery in St Helens on Tuesday. Bernie,51, slipped on the fatty snack while on his way to H Samuels to purchase a collectable porcelain green dragon. Mrs Cunliffe said \"one minute he was there discussing the local litter issues and the next he was flat on his back, pastry everywhere\". This has sparked an anti pastry campaign in the town, leading to all pasties, sausage rolls and pies being made without pastry. Jim Pickleshawl of \"Pickles Plastic Forks\" just off Jackson Street, St Helens said \"Sales have gone up, I am forking speachless\"... Police are now on the lookout for anyone with a history of disguarding pastry and claim to be closing in on a known pastry abuser from the Windle area. More details to follow next week... Submitted by Pablos Abdapolopolis"}, {"t": "Firefighters angered over council plans.", "u": "news-firefighters-angered-over-council-plans.html", "d": "9 August 2002", "x": "It seems that St Helens council and the town's fire brigade are at loggerheads over proposed new working conditions. The men and women of the brigade are angry at what they see as the council's meddling. But the council are adamant that savings have to be made - 'It's simply not cost effective', council official Kevin Slimey-Git told our reporter 'we pay these firemen and women a good bloody wage yet they actually attend a fire once or maybe twice a week. The rest of the time they spend sat around the station cooking their meals and watching TV, they even sleep on the job at nights, and as for the amount of 'naughty' calender shoots they attend, it's a scandal.' The council's chief auditor Steve Ooze also believes that change is inevitable 'The taxpayers of St Helens are getting royally ripped off by the fire service' he insists. 'It's simply a question of maths, St Helens has a large poulation of work-shy scruffy twats and unemployed single mothers who are much more deserving of the taxpayers money, all we ask of the fire service is that they consider our new working conditions, a strike would be counter-productive and could damage the brigade's reputation.' So far though the council has been vague concerning the exact form of the proposed new conditions. But the fire brigade claim to know why. 'We've seen a leaked report of the proposed changes' says Jack Handsome of the fireman's union 'and frankly it's a ***** scandal.' He continued, 'basically their plan to cut our hours and therefore our wages is simply this - they don't want us to come into work if it's raining, they think it's a waste of money to have men spraying water all over the place onto fires when the stuff's falling out of the sky.' Leading Fireman Sammy Biceps of Parr station had this to say 'my lads simply won't put up with it, they don't want to stay at home on rainy days and sit in with their wives and girlfriends, they need to be here at the station, polishing the engines, rolling the hoses, practising sliding down the pole and posing topless in their yellow pants with braces on.' He goes on 'the council seem to believe that we don't put out enough fires or something, which is a load of bollocks, only last week we had 2 plastic bins set ablaze in Haydock, one of my lads is still off sick with burns to his shaved chest after one of the bins did one of those backdraught things. And when we're not out fighting fires we have to install smoke detectors free for the grateful housewives of the borough' If the council doesn't come clean with it's plans for non-rainy day contracts then this reporter feels that it might be a very long, very hot summer."}, {"t": "Clinkham Wood - A Suburban Nature Lover's Paradise", "u": "news-clinkham-wood-a-suburban-nature-lovers-paradise.html", "d": "9 August 2002", "x": "Following last months feature on the lovely area of Parr, this month the spotlight is turned on the misrepresented suburb of Clinkham Wood. As the name suggests, the main feature of this delightful part of town is the wood itself. Steeped in history, many of the trees date back to pre-historic times and are very big with green leaves and bark on them. Relics from yesteryear are dotted around the place, including several interesting examples of charred motor vehicle remnants. Take a walk through this spectacular woodland and you might just bump into some of the friendly local characters performing their quaint traditions. Many of the younger inhabitants congregate in the beautiful surroundings, enjoying a drink or two, whilst others perform the ancient ritual of inhaling solvents for the pleasurable sensation this gives them. If you’re very lucky, you could even spot one of the few naturists who like to visit the woods on their own, surprising visitors with a quick flash of their private parts. What a hoot! Despite the abundance of nature, Clink also has some incredible examples of classic British architecture. Take a look at the wonderful example of 70s design, The Saracens Head, one of the few pubs in England which is built on stilts over a car park. The domestic residences also provide the architecturally-inquisitive a feast for the eyes, with many excellent examples of post-war prefabricated dwellings. If retail therapy is more your thing, then Clinkham Wood cannot be beaten. With not just one, but two incredible shopping centres the extensive choice is hard to take in. Whether you’re after a packet of cigs or a Pot Noodle, you’ll have no problem finding your favourite variety in Clink. Like other aspects of life in ‘the wood’, the nightlife can’t be beaten. What with the choice of the aforementioned Saracen’s Head and Moss Bank Labour club, there really is no substitute, the only criticism being the closure of the famous Banana Republic nightspot. Whatever your pleasure, Clink is the place to be."}, {"t": "Madeley back up to his old tricks - warning some people may find this offensive", "u": "news-madeley-back-up-to-his-old-tricks-warning-some-people-may-fi.html", "d": "8 August 2002", "x": "There’s an old saying the a leopard can’t change it’s spots. Although we’re not talking about acne (which can be helped by products like Clearasil and OXY 10), it seems that the smooth chat show host Richard Madeley is one permanently poxy bastard. Several years ago, Madeley was remanded in custody, and spent 6 months in Walton Prison, Liverpool, after a badly-planned robbery at Threshers Off Licence went wrong. At the time, the seemingly-sophisticated presenter tried to pass off the heist as a genuine mistake, claiming that he merely walked out with a bottle of wine after he had forgotten to pay. Now, St Helens Celebrity News can reveal that this excuse was a load of bollocks and that the scoundrel has been up to his old tricks again. A local woman (name and address withheld), was innocently out shopping in Fingerpost when she became suspicious about a tall man, fitting Madeley’s description. The woman explained ‘I was minding me own business, checkin’ out the bargains in Mr Thrifty’s, when I noticed a man who was about the same size as Richard Madeley with a balaclava on his head. I knew it was him cos he had a posh suit on, and no-one wears them round here, so I went up to him and said ‘are you Richard Madeley?’ The woman continues ‘He was dead rude. He just mumbled ‘fuck off’ through his balaclava and quickly barged his way past me. As he elbowed me, a few tins dropped on the floor, that he was hiding up his jacket. Madeley then ran towards the wine section and all hell broke loose. A far cry from his clean cut image on TV, Madeley violently grabbed the shop assistant and pulled out a sawn-off shot gun, which he had been hiding under his posh blue pinstripe suit. ‘Right you motherfuckers, get all the fucking wine in this bag now or I’ll blow all your motherfucking brains out’ Madeley screamed. In a state of panic, the shop assistant did as he said and Madelely quickly ran for the door, punching an old lady in the face as he left. Another anonymous witness saw what happened outside. ‘As Madeley rushed out of Thrifty’s he ran up to an Austin Allegro, parked on the front. And guess who was in the driving seat? Only his wife, Judy bloody Finnegan’. ‘Come on bitch’, the presenter shouted, ‘Get the motherfucking car started’. ‘Just chill bro, I’m trying to motherfucking start the motherfucker’ Judy was heard replying. With that, the Allegro spluttered into action. With a screech of brakes Finnegan quickly did a three point turn and sped off down Higher Parr Street in a cloud of fumes. Our witness added ‘As the car was driving off, Madeley could be clearly seen, leaning out of the window, with his gun pointing at the unfortunate pensioners in the queue outside the Post Office. ‘Just you motherfuckingwell try it, punks!’ he shouted aggressively as Judy waited for the lights to change. And on a flash of green, as if enough proof had not been gained, the couple sped off down Jackson Street, exactly the right way to get to the M62 and therefore, their home in London. Police are reported to be looking into the matter further, following the discovery of an abandoned Austin Allegro near Richard and Judy’s home in London."}, {"t": "Elton John shuns move to Clock Face", "u": "news-elton-john-shuns-move-to-clock-face.html", "d": "6 August 2002", "x": "The multi-millionaire and well-known uphill gardener, Elton John has shocked local residents by abandoning his planned move to the Clock Face area of St Helens. The extravagant rock star, known for his excessive spending and coke snorting blames the decision on the escalating house prices in the area. Pricey Our reporter tracked him down to his villa in Filey, Yorkshire, where the Rocket Man stated \"Yes I was planning on moving to Clock, but it's just too pricey. Property has gone through the roof just lately. I had made an offer on a lovely little cottage and then some twat went and gazumped me!\" The property in question was a two bedroomed terrace in good condition with double glazing and Economy 7 heating. Elton was reported to have 'fallen in love' with the area after waking up in a local hairdresser's bed after a bender at Flex, Cotham Street. However, friends of the glamour queen have suggested a more sinister theory to the reason for his change of plans. One insider said \"it's that David Furnish. Elton's well under the thumb with him.\" Furnish, originally from Wigan, has allegedly put the blockers on the couples move because he doesn't like the pies in St Helens! Shite Once again, our reporter set about finding the truth. After days of tracking down the former welder, Furnish was spotted in a nightclub in Leigh. Eventually, he cracked and admitted \"Yes, alright it's true, Pimmies pies are shite!\""}, {"t": "STUDENT IN PIE SHOCK HORROR PROBE SENSATION", "u": "news-student-in-pie-shock-horror-probe-sensation.html", "d": "31 July 2002", "x": "A St Helens College student was said to be ‘severely shocked and embarrassed’ today after a horror incident round the back of the Nat West Bank. Our reporter caught up with student Hercules Mc Aspirin as he recovered at home. Hercules, who is studying GNVQ in Pub Singing (with Karaoke options), was still visibly shaken as he described his ordeal. “I was walking towards the college entrance eating a Galloway’s Chunky Steak Pie, when I suddenly tripped. The pie flew out of my hand and to my horror I saw it fly through the air and land straight in a litter bin! It was awful…I’ve never been so f*****n shocked in my life. I had to go and buy another one to throw on the street.”"}, {"t": "News in Brief", "u": "news-news-in-brief.html", "d": "30 July 2002", "x": "Looked at Funny A man was looked at in a funny way in Church Street, last Saturday. The victim, whose name has been withheld for his own safety said, \"this bloke definitely looked at me funny\". Police are said to be taking the matter very seriously. Cat up tree A cat was stuck up a tree for two weeks in Sutton recently. However, when the fire brigade eventually pulled the furry feline to safety, RSPCA inspectors revealed that it was in fact an 'Ecuadorian Lesser-Spotted Tree Frog', not a cat. Parr Rumour A vicious rumour has been sweeping the town. The rumour was that 'Parr is nice'. Our reporters quickly went to Parr to check out the story. On returning to the office, they confirmed that it was 'just a rumour'. Newton le Willows Education Initiative A new education initiative is being introduced to raise local awareness in the schools of Newton le Willows. The aim of the scheme is to educate the pupils into realising that the town is part of the St Helens Borough. Unfortunately, the students got off to a bad start, as none of them had actually heard of St Helens. Pint Spilled A local man had his pint spilled in Nexus Nightclub on Saturday night. Unfortunately the offender managed to run off before his victim had the chance to confront him. Any information about this incident can be emailed to the SHCN office. This information will then be passed on to the man who had his pint spilled in order to arrange the mandatory 'twatting'. Woman Embarrassed An unnamed woman was said to be 'highly embarrassed' yesterday. Whilst queuing at the checkout in Asda, she was reported to have farted and inadvertently 'followed through'."}, {"t": "Billinge or Broke - Bin Laden's been Busted", "u": "news-billinge-or-broke-bin-ladens-been-busted.html", "d": "30 July 2002", "x": "Big bad bearded bastard, Bin Laden bobbed (that's enough alliteration, Ed.) through the crowds of Billinge High Street almost unnoticed yesterday. Despite his long flowing beard, his AK47 assault rifle and the 'trademark' tea towel on his head, this was the last place people would expect him to hide. However, according to local historian Greg Frogmarch, there's a very plausible explanation. Several years ago, Frogmarch went off to explore the nearby Crank Caverns with his mate Trevor (from the Foresters pub), an Ever-Ready torch and a packed lunch. Despite leaving at 10am, by 11pm they had not returned. Understandably worried, Frogmarch's wife, Vera phoned the police who began to search the caves. Two weeks later the search was called off with no sign of the explorers. Bizarrely, a week after the hunt had been abandoned, Vera received a phone call from Kabul, Afghanistan. It was Greg. Lost in the intricate network of caves, Greg and Trevor spent three harrowing weeks in a desparate battle for survival. Living on a ration of one Quaver per day and an ever-depleting carton of Sunny Delight (Florida Style), the pair clawed their wayto onwards and onwards. Eventually, having almost lost the will to live, they spotted a tiny ray of sunlight at the end of another seemingly endless dirty tunnel. Shadows of their former selves, they emerged, scarred and bruised, ragged and torn in the Tora Bora mountains. Luckily, they managed to bribe a Taliban soldier with their remaining Quavers to smuggle them onto a plane back from Afghanistan to London. \"When I got home, I thought no more about it\" says Greg, \"It wasn't until I saw someone fitting Bin Laden's description in Threshers, buying 20 Regal, that I put two and two together. It's all too obvious now. Me and Trev had stumbled upon Al Quaeda's escape route from Afghanistan.\" Corroborative evidence has also come to light from Dave Wagstaff of Pocket Nook, who claims to have seen a man fitting the terrorist's description cavorting with two unknown women in Nexus nightclub, Westfield Street."}, {"t": "Parr - take a fresh look", "u": "news-parr-take-a-fresh-look.html", "d": "28 July 2002", "x": "To many people, Parr in St Helens might not be their ideal choice of a tourist destination, but if you scratch below the surface, you’ll find that there’s far more to this overlooked area than meets the eye. The quaint suburb of Parr lies approximately 1 mile east of St Helens Town Centre, with it’s historic centre and vibrant nightlife. Follow the signs to Newton le Willows from the town centre and you’ll soon arrive in the semi-rural idyll that is Parr. More of a rustic village than a suburb, Parr offers a tranquillity that helps the weary traveller forget about all the cares of the world. Take a look around the ‘period style’ shops and marvel at the charming crafts and curios that are displayed in the windows. Why not visit one of the areas many famous hostelries, such as the Hen and Chickens or the Blood Tub, for a relaxing drink or meal with friends or chill out in the cool waters of Parr baths. For the nature lovers out there, Parr certainly won’t leave you disappointed. Why not take a stroll along the banks of ‘Stinky Brook’where you’ll find several varieties of wild flowers and other items. Breathe in the clear air and wonder at the joy of being alive in such a wonderful place. For the more adventurous tourists, there are lots of action sports that you can participate in. Regular motor cycle events are held on the local fields. Just bring your own motorbike, or ‘borrow one’ from the generous locals. If cars are more your thing, historically-traditional races are regularly staged, where the locals race around the locality in an attempt to ‘out-wit’ the local constabulary. Once again, vehicles can be ‘borrowed’ from around the area to enable you to join in these exciting activities. Having enjoyed a relaxing or exciting day, once the sun goes down, Parr really comes alive. Near to the area’s ancient wine merchants, you will see many of the younger locals enjoying chatting together and catching up on the days activities, whilst the adults prefer to sup a small glass of the local speciality beverages before retiring to bed after an action packed day. Alternatively, if you like to be entertained, why not take in a show at one of the famous Labour clubs? You’ll be amazed at the quality of the artists, and all at a price that will suit the pocket. Whatever your taste, we’re sure that you’ll find what your looking for in the beautiful place that is Parr."}, {"t": "Simon Cowell shagged my Mum", "u": "news-simon-cowell-shagged-my-mum.html", "d": "26 July 2002", "x": "Imagine having to cook breakfast for a well-known celebrity. Difficult one eh? Well that’s what happened to young Arnold Smeggytits (21) from Peasley Cross last week. Arnold, a catering student at St Helens College was gobsmacked when he realised the identity of the star in question and was given little time to prepare for the arduous task ahead. “Me Mam quite often cops off with A-list celebrities ‘cos of her big tits and that” Arnold explained, “But this time was different and I wasn’t ready for the challenge that lay ahead.” “I was going to go for a slash, when I could hear someone whistling Will Young’s ‘Evergreen’ in the bathroom. I waited outside the door for the bloke to finish having a shit. Then I heard the chain flush and he opened the door. And guess who it was? Only Simon bloody Cowell from Pop Idol”. Apparently, the razor-tongued svengali, who owns a property on the exclusive Shires development, had been drinking in the Chicago Rock Café, when he homed in on Arnold’s Mum, Eva Smeggytits. Within no time, Eva had grabbed his bollocks and dragged him back to her modest two-up two-down, without even stopping off for a split and gravy. “I did hear someone come in,” Arnold continued “but they went straight to the bedroom. All I could hear was the bed creaking and me Mam shouting “spank me you bastard”.” But the real test of manhood was yet to come. “Arnold, get your arse down that shop and get some bacon and eggs for our Si”, Eva shouted from the bedroom. Arnold did as he was told and returned in anticipation of his task. On returning to the house, he found that Cowell had made himself at home and was sitting back watching Danii Behr on telly with his feet on the coffee table. “Get that breakfast cooked now you little shit”, Cowell barked. “And it had better be good.” “I was brickin' meself”, admitted Arnold. “they don’t prepare you for this at College”. The first thing to go wrong was the eggs. Instead of being nice and white, Arnold had the gas too high and the bottom went all brown and crispy. The bacon wasn’t much better and the poor lad went and burned the toast. In an attempt to cover-up the error, Arnold frantically scraped the burnt bits off the toast and quickly delivered the results to the impatient millionaire in the next room. “What the FUCK is this?” Cowell screamed, his face turning a shade of purple. “Bacon and eggs” Arnold replied in a quivering voice. “Bacon and eggs?” the high-waised one blurted. “Do you think people will ever want to eat the shite you make? Do you seriously think you’ve got what it takes to be a chef? You must be fucking mental, you pathetic little loser, you shit stain on the arse of humanity. Don’t EVER cook anything again. You will NEVER, repeat NEVER make it as a chef” Cowell ranted. And with that, Cowell stormed out of the house and screeched off in his black Ferrari, showing a two-fingered salute to Arnold as he watched through the window. As if that wasn’t enough, Arnold then got twatted round the head by his Mum. “You useless prick, I was hoping Simon was going to start seeing me proper.” “Bastard men!” Arnold has now booked in for therapy and is changing courses to motor vehicle maintenance. Eva is now reported to be seeing Dr Fox."}, {"t": "Johnny Vegas in Background Shocker", "u": "news-johnny-vegas-in-background-shocker.html", "d": "25 July 2002", "x": "Unfortunate news for St Helens has recently been reported the the SHCN office. It appears that the big-bellied, beer swilling comedian, known as Johnny Vegas is an imposter. Despite his claims to have been brought up in an impoverished working class family in Thatto Heath, it appears that the truth is a long way from such a humble background. Having been given a tip off in The Brown Edge pub, our reporter tracked down Vegas to his luxury apartment in Belgravia, London. Vegas, whose real name is Michael Piers Montmorency Pennington-Smythe answered the door wearing a velvet smoking jacket, cravate and monacle, a far cry from his usual scruffy appearance. At first he was shocked by our discovery but after some considerable persuasion, the charlatan agreed to come clean. Educated at Eton and subsequently a classics scholar at Oxford, Vegas speaks with an upper-class accent, not unlike Prince Charles. \"Oh Crikey\" he says \"it appears that you chappies have rumbled my jolly good scam\". Apparently Vegas got the idea for his character whilst attending a dinner party with his good friend Shaun Woodward (millionaire MP for St Helens South). Vegas explains \"Woody and I had consumes a tad too much Champers that evening and he was joking about these funny little northern types and how pathetic they behave. He called them \"sub-human underclass wankers\". So that's when I came up with the idea of Johnny\". Vegas researched his character by taking a first class train journey to Liverpool Lime Street and then getting on the train to St Helens Central. By accident, he got off the train one stop too early and found himself in Thatto Heath. \"It was rather surreal\", he continues \"I'd never seen such a fucking dump in my whole life\". Vegas quickly picked up the local accent after the ticket attendant threaned to 'twat' him for talking posh. In an attempt to perfect the northern slob image, Johnny spent as much time as possible in the areas pubs getting completely shit-faced. \"I studied the locals in the pubs and developed my character from the miserable existences that they carve out for themselves. Then I developed my stage act which, ironically, allows me to profit financially from these poor bastards misery. I'd call it Pure Genius, ha,ha,ha\" he chortles."}, {"t": "It's all going off up Four Acre", "u": "news-its-all-going-off-up-four-acre.html", "d": "25 July 2002", "x": "Following the acrimonious split between Tom Cruise and Nicole Kidman, it's no secret that they've both been putting it about a bit. What with Tom shagging anything in a skirt and Nicole's penchant for younger men like Robbie Williams and Russell Crowe, friction has been running high on the Four Acre estate, Sutton. It's common knowledge that both sets of parents of the former couple have lived in relative harmony on the estate, until recently, where the couple's post-marital antics are said to be causing severe ructions. Relationships have become even more strained since Tom Cruise was forced to move back in with his mam, after his latest maud, Penelope Cruz 'packed him in'. \"Our Tom was gutted,\" explains Rene Cruise, \"He's a sensitive lad really, but ever since he split up with that bitch, Nicole, he's gone off the rails. He's down that Green Dragon, pissed every night and sometimes even goes to the Smithy Manor for a fight.\" As our reporter was talking to Rene, he heard a shout from the bottom of the street. It was Nicole's mum, Elsie. \"Hey you, yer slag. Don't you go callin' our Nicole, it's your Tom who can't keep his dick in his pants.\" No sooner had Elsie Kidman appeared than Rene Cruise legged it down the street with a rolling pin shouting \"Everyone knows where she gets it from, you've had more cock than Pimmies sell pies, you fookin' whoore!\" At that point, Tom Cruise came sprinting out of his mam's house in his string vest and Y fronts. \"Pack it in mam, she's not worth it\" he shouted, pulling the battling pensioners off each other. \"Yes she is\", Rene cried, \"I'll bloody-well swing for her!\" Eventually Tom managed to calm things down, and the net curtains gradually stopped twitching. \"It's alright, our Mam, I'm not arsed about that Nicole any more. I met a well-fit bird in the Sidac club on Friday night, so you don't have to be mithered any more.\" \"I hope she's not one of them dirty slappers like you normally bring home, our Tom\", Rene said, \"No mam, she gets her hair bleached at the hairdressers and even washes her fanny every day, not like that Nicole\". \"Ah, I'm made up for yer, our Tom, now get your arse down that Chippy and bring us a split and gravy, twice, for us tea.\" \"Nice one Mam\", chuckled Tom. On returning to the office, our reporter phoned Nicole Kidman's manager for her comments on the events. Nicole is said to be 'non-plussed' with the situation in Four Acre and is going to send Robbie Williams round to Tom's house to twat him."}, {"t": "Jamie Oliver Acquires Spicey Chicken", "u": "news-jamie-oliver-acquires-spicey-chicken.html", "d": "25 July 2002", "x": "Top TV chef and self-styled jack-the-lad, Jamie Oliver has recently bought the long-standing home of culinary excellence, The Spicy Chicken in St Helens. The cheeky cockney had been interested in the establishment ever since his recent visit to the town for a night out. Oliver, originally from Fingerpost, returned to the town to attend a stag night for his mate, Daz Flangefettler. \"Me and Daz got up to some serious malarkey that night\", the chef quipped in confidence, \"I hope Jules doesn't find out what we were up to, suffice to say that it involved three birds from Pocket Nook, a tub of raspberry ripple ice cream, a policeman's truncheon and a ferret.\" \"On our way home, we called in at the Spicy Chicken for some tukka. And I'll tell you what, it was fackin' pukka tukka, my son\". In fact, Oliver was so impressed with the purveyors of poultry that, the next day, he got straight on the blower to Norman Wankmeister the shop's owner. At first, proud owner Wankmeister was very reluctant to let the takeaway go, as he was so attached to it. However, on hearing the TV celebrity's extravagant offer, Norman was overheard saying that he \"couldn't give a shit about the place\". Oliver's PR people in London have been hard at workpromoting his new venture. \"Jamie's made up with buying the Spicy Chicken and he's got some great ideas about developing the business. He's thinking of changing the name to fit in with the times, and we've already developed a new sign for the outside. I hope you 'Tellinsers will appreciate the changes, only time will tell.\" The 'new look' Spicy Chicken Jamie Oliver is also in negotiations with Larkins, North Road, St Helens."}, {"t": "Belgium Correspondent – Bri", "u": "world-belgium.html", "d": "2002", "x": "The Missus moved out here in 1999 because of her job. Being on the old “Rock & Roll” at the time and not having played any for a while I decided to join her. The only thing I knew about the place was that in Belgium they speak French & Dutch and that Liége is in the French-speaking part. I now know a lot more about the place… Liege is “SPECIAL” as the French say, this is a catch-all term to mean everything from daft-as-a-brush to funny-peculiar. It has a population that is 40% Italian and 100% party animal. Unlike their Flemish cousins the Liégeois embrace the Latin culture which means spending the annual budget on street parties instead of roads and lounging around café terraces drinking Pastis with a Salvador Dali moustache. At times the place borders on Latin America with its cultural mix of inhabitants and if there seems to be a world shortage of supermodels it’s ‘cos there all here. Jaw-droppingly gorgeous women shimmy around the streets everywhere you look. Stella Artois (40p a can from the supermarket) is brewed just up the road in nearby Leuven but no bugger drinks it ‘cos the local beer JUPILER pisses all over it. In fact when it comes to beer the Belgians rule, not just because of the dazzling number of types they produce but because they have cracked the problem of brewing 9% (and stronger) that doesn’t taste like treacle mixed with WD40. One of our local bars has 900 beers in stock, 30 on draught. All in all there’s never a dull moment, whether it’s a palm tree mysteriously appearing in the town square or the Tour De France passing through, and as Holland is 20 minutes away (Maastricht - see photo of the Carnival- MENTAL) we can easily buy magic mushrooms over the counter…not that you need them in Liége . And I still can’t persuade me mates to visit… Bri"}, {"t": "Italy Correspondent – Pete & Gary", "u": "world-italy.html", "d": "2002", "x": "There are two of us Sint Ellins lads out here in Livorno. We're both here showing these Italians how to play rugby. They seem to be playing a poof's version of the game. You know how football players throw themselves on the floor after every tackle and roll around and argue with the ref, well imagine that but with an oval ball. Gary has been here for two years now and has bagged himself a decent maud. She makes good pasta but a crap split and fish - you can't have it all! He can speak the language, which helps as he's now the coach of the team. But you'll be pleased to know that his inspirational team talks are just stories of how Roy Haggerty \"knocked lads about and that\". I came out here back in November, after Gary called me up because he needed a back row player. I've got the basics of the language (\"Uno d'ogni, per favore cara?\" \"One of each, please love?\" - unfortunately the Pimblett's empire has not stretched this far), but it still needs work. We spend most of our free time having a look round Tuscany, drinking wine, and eating various cheeses. We also squeeze in the odd skiing session with the occasional BBQ down on the beach here and there. The wine here is absolutely lovely, they're the world champions at making it or something. As a consequence the beer is shite. The general stereo-type of Italians being soft and vain, in our opinion, is absolutely bang on. They are always swanning about with the perfect hair and clothes which can only be described as \"dead good\". When they go out they only have one or two glasses of wine and perhaps a coffee. They never get bladdered, like normal people. We've got a mate out here though, Federico, who came to St.Helens for a visit over Christmas. He's the best Italian we've found. Likes his piss, not that arsed about how he looks, and loves Nexus! Peter & Gary, Livorno, Tuscany, Italy"}, {"t": "South Africa Correspondent – James", "u": "world-southafrica.html", "d": "2002", "x": "I always wanted to say \"its hell in the colonies\" but I would have been about twenty years too late. The closest I could have got in 1979 when we arrived here was \"Its hell in the former colonies\" but you must admit it doesn't have the same ring to it. When I say we, I mean me andt missus, Gaynor. Scousers as we all know are very clever and Gaynor is no exception to this rule. She is unlike your average Scouser in one way though, She admits that she was not in The Cavern on the night that The Beatles performed for the very first time. I have yet to meet another Scouser who readily admits to this, the place must be massive. She does however insist that she has stood in the Kop and I occasionally pretend that I believe her to keep the peace or when I want my own way. Having now established who the \"we\" is I will now get back to hell and the colonies. It would be easy to tell you about the beautiful beaches of Cape Town and Durban but if you want to know about that then get the buzz to town and annoy a travel agent by pretending you want to go there, I am sure you can get a brochure. I would much rather tell you what it is really like living 8000 miles away from Hardshaw Street and what the people are like. First the people. South Africa as we know are very good at splitting people into groups and not wishing to try and reinvent the wheel I will do the same. The largest group is of course the indigenous one, the Africans. On the whole, these are very pleasant people who get on with life and try and do the best they can. There is however a section of that group, like other groups who like to indulge in crime and even if they didn't would get the blame anyway. Car hijackings and robbery seem to be the required method of wealth creation of that group and they are fairly successful at it. So successful in fact that the newspapers don't even report it anymore, every one does however know a close friend or colleague who has been hijacked. The African male in general is soccer mad. Talking about and playing soccer is a major social past time. When the riots of 1976 were at there height many in the army and police believed that the best way to stop the fighting would be to throw a football into the crowd and then every one would just get on with a game instead, forget the fighting and go home after ninety minuets. I don't think theory was ever actually tested though. The next major group are Afrikaans. These are the people that the British Government gave power over too when they pulled out. On the whole they are pleasant enough but have a patriotism which borders on the unhealthy. Nowadays this patriotism is directed at sport. Every one is a rugby and cricket fanatic, young,old,male and female. Should the national side at these sports be beaten they genuinely and sincerely believe that it is the fault of the referee on umpire, The whole loss is due to a major conspiracy that the rest of the World has against them because if all way fair, then they are unbeatable purely due to the fact that they are South African and for no other reason at all. Hansie Cronje's bribe taking was the G7's conspiracy to weaken South African cricket. The group which is the smallest but as ever has the biggest mouth is of course the immigrants. Around twenty five percent of this group consists of our countryman. I have learned over the years that a large proportion of this group are in fact the kind of people that I left England to get away from, but they cannot always be avoided. These people generally \"buy\" into the South African way of life and in a attempt to fit in at any cost, will support South Africa against any opposition, including The English. I personally have no time for these people and it is convenient that in general they tend to be scousers. This allows me to kill two birds with one stone. A lot of them belong to Liverpool supporters clubs and meet regulalarly at appropriate venues where they also vent there anger against referees should there team lose, funny that. The rest of us who do remain patriotic are known not too affectionately as Souties. This is a Afrikaans term and implies that you don't really know which country you are living in and have one foot in England and the other in South Africa. Your balls are therefore hanging in the salty sea, clever eh. James"}, {"t": "Russia Correspondent – Woden", "u": "world-russia.html", "d": "2002", "x": "Spring has sprung in this land that W.S.Churchill once describedas“an enigma, wrapped in a riddle, wrapped in a mystery” - or words to that effect. What the fuck was he on about, I wonder? Another observer of Russian mores - one Madame de Stael, I think - said “Russia is a land of secrets, where there are, however, no secrets.” I think I might just know what she was getting at. When I arrived here in 1989 the USSR was in its death throes, though nobody knew of this at the time. The parlous state of the Soviet Ship of State notwithstanding, those fun lovin’ lads n’ lasses in the KGB were still going full steam ahead in their sworn undertaking to defend Soviet internal security. One of their chief activities at that time was to latch onto any small incident, no matter how trivial, in which a Westerner was involved, in the hopes of magnifying said incident out of all proportion, thereby enabling them to put the frighteners on some poor bastard so as to blackmail him or make him more amenable to any shady proposal that they may at some time suggest to him. Twats! April 11, 1990. My birthday. Voronezh, central European Russia. Perestroika is in full swing. There’s fuck all in the shops and Gorbachev has cut down on vodka production and sales and hiked its price. Everybody is really fucking well pissed off because they can no longer get pissed up. And everybody’s skint - bar yours truly! Being a student at Voronezh State University, I was getting a grant off the Soviet Union to the tune of 400 RUR a month. The average grant received by Russian Students at that time was 30 RUR! The only bright note at that time was the Lambada. Russia was undergoing a Lambada craze. All bastard day you could hear its strains, see its videos on the TV. Lads used to stand with permanent hards-on, ogling at the TV screens in cafes and bars, totally gobsmacked at the raw sexuality of this dance. FUCKIN’ DISGUSTIN’!!! So I decide to book a banquet at the newest hotel in town. I paid top price and ordered the best grub and invited my best Russian buddies and the nicest pussy in town. There were about 40 guests in all. It was the best party anyone could ever remember and it cost me 36 quid in total - a king’s ransom for Russkies then! Everyone got steamin’ and everyone was dancing the Lambada like it was going out of fashion. Around 11 pm, the cops started drifting in. It used to be lights out at 9 pm, those days. Thinking I was a foreign businessman and not a student (I hate fuckin’ students, me!), they didn’t quite know what to do, but they were none too happy because people were CLEARLY ENJOYING THEMSELVES!! Then I made my big mistake. It was Easter Saturday and suddenly I come over all religious and decide to go to midnight mass, as I’m a sucker for Russian Orthodox Church choirs. As soon as I had cleared the scene, the cops came in heavy handed on the boys and the shit really hit the fan. Knives were drawn, dogs set loose, twattin’ sticks were twattin’ and warning shots were fired as the cops read the riot act. Many arrests were made. I was arrested the following morning just after I’d got me leg over in a sobering up exercise. Although they codded on that they were detectives, it soon became clear that my interrogators were boys from the KGB. Slowly, slowly they began to up the intimidation stakes. I had to make a confession that I’d “organised acts of hooliganism” - a serious offence in the USSR. I’d get a year for that if I confessed, as the judge would be sympathetic for my avoiding time wasting, they told me. They gave me a statement to sign. It was written in Russian. I demanded a translation. That’d take several days, they rejoindered. The interview had so far been in English by means of a translator who spoke in Dickensian English. The British Embassy here always advises that if you get in trouble, never sign anything and demand an interpreter. And if it be the case, you should also never let them know you can speak Russian. Making no progress, they started being smarmy: “We can see you’re an intellectual…” “Clearly, you are an English gentleman…” and, believe it or not, “We do so admire your Mrs. Thatcher…”! In the end, they began to lose their rag. “ Listen,” they said, “if you don’t sign this, you’ll end up getting 5 years.” “Five years!” I say. “What for?” “One year for organising hooliganism, another for causing criminal damage, another year for threatening the manager, another year for threatening the police, and finally,” added the chief joker and the smarmiest of them all (there were 3 of them), “one year for rude and immodest dancing.” “I don’t get you,” I said disbelievingly, “What are you on about? I can’t dance to save my life!” “You were dancing the Lambada,” says snidey chops with a sneer. “Yeah, like the whole of Russia has been doing for the past year?” say I, “So what’s the big deal?” “But you were dancing the ENGLISH Lambada!” he concludes triumphantly. “Fuck me!” I think, “Salt mines here I come!” So then I drop bollock number two in this saga. I say to them in Russian, “Well, if I get banged up here for five, I’ll come out speaking fluent Russian!” They go fuckin’ berserk! “You can speak Russian!” they shout. “Why didn’t you tell us you can speak Russian?” “You never asked,” I say nonchalantly. Snidey chop’s face turns puce. “How much of our conversation could you understand?” he shouts at me. “About 70%” I say, lying through my teeth. I’ve got them on the defensive now. The ball’s in my court. They suddenly metamorphose into Mr. Nice Guys. They tell me I’m free to go for the time being, that they’ll have a talk with the investigatory judge to see if they can get me off with a year in jug - or even with only a fine. They say they’ll telephone me in a few days. A few days pass. My best mate, Ivan, puts me in the picture. He tells me they’re just trying to put the frighteners on me and that I’d done very well - so far. “They’ll ask you for a present, next,” says Ivan, “Give them nowt. And don’t agree to meet them alone. Always have at least two witnesses if you must see them. Best not arrange to meet them at all. Just keep on fuckin’ them off and then they’ll get pissed off and leave you alone. But if you start dancing to their tune, they’ll never be off your back.” And this is just what I do. A few days later, snidey chops rings. He tells me the room number of a hotel where he and his two other stooges wish to “interview” me again. “And don’t forget,” he says, “the day of the interview is my birthday!” “Fuck you!” I think, and on the day of the meeting I don’t turn up. Another day passes. Another phone call. It’s my friend snidey chops again. “Did you forget about your interview, Woden?” he says. “No,” I reply. “So why didn’t you come, Woden?” he enquires, adopting a hurt tone. “Listen,” I say, “there’s no way I’m going to take part in secret meetings with you and your colleagues. The only possibility of my meeting you is on condition that I have present with me at least two witnesses.” “You haven’t told anybody about our proposed meetings, have you?” he hisses. “No,” I lie, “not up to now.” “Good,” he continues, adopting his smarmy tone once again. “And why all this talk of ‘secret meetings’, Woden? We don’t want to hold secret meetings! Just don’t tell anyone about them.” Amazed by the Orwellian doublethink of the KGB, I agree to meet them again, but once more, I don’t turn up. I heard nothing more off them after that. They call themselves the FSB now. (Federalnaya slyzhba bezopasnosti - Federal Security Service) I wonder if they’ve changed tactics? Somehow, I don’t think so. Woden The God Not long after I had decided to settle down here in Moscow, I bought a biography of Joseph Stalin. I had gone into a bookshop on Tverskaya Street simply to browse and, quite by chance, had called in on the very day when sales of the biography had begun. The author of the book was there, signing copies of his work. Neatly arranged on several long shelves were stacked copies of his latest work, and in front of the shelves stood two very bored shop assistants. They were both young and beautiful. Russia has a surfeit of beautiful women. Most Westerners, I believe, think that all Russian women are dowdy, fat, frumpy peasants who have become prematurely aged and embittered as a result of their relentless struggle to live and simply to survive in ‘the Evil Empire of the East’ (as an erstwhile president of the United States and former Hollywood B-movie actor once described the Soviet Union). This stereotypical Femina Sovietica was partly the result of the fact that the wives of Soviet Communist leaders were, in the main, dowdy, fat, frumpy peasant babyshki. However, Western propaganda is the chief reason why this cartoon-character, stereotypical Russian woman existed and, to a large extent, still exists now. In the simple world of simple, unthinking folk ‘good’ means ‘beautiful’, ‘bad’ means ‘ugly’. For the ‘West’ read ‘good’; for ‘Russia’ read ‘Evil’! Ergo -Westerners are beautiful and Russians are ugly. Interestingly, before the Russian Revolution - or to be more precise, before ‘The Great October Bolshevik Revolution’ - Westerners considered Russian women to be the desirable, exotic, ‘semi-Asiatic’ creatures that they indeed really are. Moreover, to a fortunate few Westerners resident in the former Soviet Union (including myself) this judgement is acknowledged fact. This can be easily ascertained by anyone who has time to browse through the baleful appeals for Russian wives written by American businessmen and which appear daily in the Moscow English language press ‘Lonely Hearts’ columns. But I digress; two exceptional beauties stood motionlessly before me like two life-like mannequins in some expensive Paris couturier’s shop window. Hanging on the bookshelves in this section, which was solely devoted to the sale of the new Stalin biography, were two cards showing two different prices. “How much does the biography of Stalin cost?” I asked. “Can’t you read?” snorted one of the krasavitsa contemptuously. I hesitated momentarily, quickly trying to compose in my head a suitable sarcastic and pithy response. All that I could muster was: “I’m sorry. I’ve forgotten my glasses.” No doubt recognising by my accent that I was a foreigner (my enquiry about the price of the book must have been made in flawless Russian - but then, you ask the price of things every day!), her attitude immediately changed. “Oh, I’m terribly sorry!” she said, genuinely apologetically. “And besides,” I added, “there are two prices shown on your shelves.” “Are there really?” she said, turning around to look at the bookshelves. Her interest in me was now being shared by her workmate who, until then, had shown complete indifference to me, my enquiries - to everything and everyone! She had remained standing there motionless and magnificently beautiful, utterly contemptuous of all around her. My surprise at the shop assistant’s downright rude reply quickly turned to anger. This anger rapidly became more intense as the two young women began openly to fawn upon me quite simply because I was a Westerner. The shop assistant’s vulgar response to my polite question had abruptly extinguished all my other thoughts. I wanted to say to them: “Is it too difficult for you to be polite? Why are you so bloody rude to me? What have I done to you that causes you to be so nasty to me?” I said nothing. They told me the price of the book and by screwing up my eyes and peering intently at the price tags on the shelves, I pretended that I really did have difficulty in reading them at that distance. I bought the book. Outside I began to think about what I should have said to the two bad mannered young women. “I should have asked them why they were so uncultured,” I thought to myself, composing a Russian sentence in my mind. ‘Nekyltyrno!’ I thought in Russian - a favourite Russian pejorative meaning far more than ‘uncultured’, having in addition overtones of ‘vulgar’, ‘uneducated’, ‘base’… And so seething with anger, whilst at the same time composing a grammatically perfect Russian sentence expressing what I should have said but did not, in fact, say to the two rude young women, I proceeded down Tverskaya towards the Kremlin. How many times have I become so irate in this country over such boorish behaviour exhibited by the natives? How many times must I fume and rage over such meaningless trivialities concerning manners, etiquette, and normal, so-called ‘civilised’ behaviour? I have chosen to live in this land. I have lived here for several years now. I ought to have become accustomed to all of this alien behaviour. However, I have not. I am a foreigner here; I am an Englishman. Is that the reason for my irritability over this matter? Do I, as a foreigner, have the right to impose my mores onto those who have been raised in quite a different society to that in which I was reared and educated? Russians, like all other nations, have stereotypical images of the natives of other lands. In common with every one else, it seems the Russian idea of a typical Englishman is personified in the form of the master sleuth, Sherlock Holmes. Sir Arthur Conan-Doyle’s most famous character is for most Russians the epitome of Englishness. Holmes is a tall, slim, handsome, English gentleman whose eccentricity only adds a certain piquancy to his perfect charm, good manners, and gentility. He is a highly educated, shrewd, percipient and intelligent man. Above all, he is cultured. Holmes, the typical Englishman, is, in short, everything, which most Russians hold themselves not to be. Russians even sometimes take some pride in the fact that they are personified by the bear - a rough, shambling brute of a creature, which at first sight may appear to be a stupid and docile beast but which in reality possesses tremendous strength that can be used aggressively to a terrifying degree. Several years ago I was returning on the night train to Moscow from the city of Voronezh, a journey of some three hundred miles that lasts for twelve hours. It was mid-winter and the temperature was minus 25?C. Before going to sleep, my Russian travelling companion (who was my first Russian woman friend) had told me not to converse with any passenger who might enter our six-berth compartment during the course of our journey. The reason for this advice was to avoid any possible confrontation with the carriage guard. I had purchased my ticket under false pretences, travelling incognito as the spouse of my companion. This subterfuge was simply undertaken to avoid the fare demanded of Westerners. Russian citizens and foreigners pay different tariffs on the Russian railway system. If the guard had discovered that I had deceived her, there may have been hell to pay. On entering the carriage at Voronezh railway station I had, therefore, not said a word, silently carrying my ‘wife’s’ suitcase, and playing the role of the strong, silent, dutiful spouse. At about three in the morning the train made a scheduled stop at some God-forsaken spot in the middle of nowhere. The weather had been deteriorating all night and as I gazed out of the window from my upper bunk, I could barely discern a handful of people struggling along the platform manhandling their luggage in a raging blizzard. I had been unable to go to sleep. I have never been able to sleep on a Russian train. In winter, it is always too cold for me to sleep and in summer too hot. As the train slowly pulled out of the station into the pitch-black, snow-swept night, a man in his sixties entered our compartment, which up to then had only been occupied by my companion and me. After he had removed his gloves, fur hat, scarf and heavy, winter overcoat, I could see that he was wearing the uniform of the Soviet Railways. He was probably a locomotive driver returning to Moscow after completing his work schedule. He did not remove his ‘valenki’, felt boots worn in winter and which are, in my opinion, the best kind of footwear for Russian winters. He did not lie down on the free bunk that he had chosen as his own, but simply sat down and, seeing that I was awake, began to converse with me. “Zdravstvyitye!”, he said. I replied likewise. He continued to converse with me about our journey to Moscow, the weather - about everything in general and nothing in particular. In short, he behaved like a typical English gentleman, being continuously gracious and polite and showing no indication whatsoever of any irritation that he may have felt towards my almost monosyllabic responses to his enquiries and observations. Our strange conversation continued for along time until finally the elderly Russian railway worker finally posed the question that I had long been expecting. “You’re not Russian, are you?” he said. “No.” “Are you from The Baltic States?” “No.” There was for the first time during the course of this almost one-sided conversation a momentary silence on the part of my interlocutor. I felt embarrassed. For a little while I pondered whether to reveal to him the truth of my identity. In the end I confessed: “As a matter of fact, I’m English.” “English!” he said, with great surprise. “English!” he repeated with an air of disbelief. “English! England!! Such a cultured land!” We both fell into silence and eventually went asleep facing each other on opposite bunks in a sitting position as the train slowly jolted and rattled its way across the snow-swept Russian heartland northwards towards Moscow. Much later, as the train was approaching the outskirts of the capital, my companion awoke. After first greeting her and introducing himself, the Russian railwayman informed her with barely veiled excitement: “Do you know, our sputnik is English! What a wonderful, cultured people! Such a cultured society! How awful it must be for him to be here in Russia! Compared to the English we Russians are so…so, well…so uncultured!” That same female travelling companion later lived in sin with me in St.Helens. At that time I was studying as a postgraduate at Manchester University. I, therefore, had to often leave her alone for the greater part of the day in my former residence situated in the now infamous Clinkham Wood drug ghetto. One evening I returned home to find her in tears. It seemed that she had decided to take stroll around the Dam in the afternoon and had been confronted by gobshites wagging it from school. They’d demanded cigs off her and, on hearing her accent, wanted to know where she was from. On learning her nationality, they’d said her: “Fuck off back to Russia, you foreign slag!” “Woden”, she tearfully asked me, “what does ‘slag’ mean?” Such friendly folk, St.Helensers! Woden the God"}, {"t": "Spain Correspondent – Sharky", "u": "world-spain.html", "d": "2002", "x": "Well i have to say firstly that i am leaving this lovely place soon cause i am off to work in the south of France for the summer with some frogs. But i have been living here for 9 months and i know enough to tell you about this Catalan city. Barcelona, is case you didn’t know, is in Catalunia which is quite different to the rest of Spain. It is an autonomy which basically means they sort out their own shit and don’t get bossed around by Madrid. I hate to spoil the myth that Spain = hot but it just isn’t true. Fair enough the average temperature in Summer is sbout 30º but in winter its a nice and brisk 10º. Not helped by the fact that Spaniards do not seem to be aware of the existence of carpet or central heating! Not like the comforts of Billinge i can tell you. If you like art, this is the place to come. There is psychadelic Gaudi shit everywhere and plenty of tourists to take pictures of it. It is a very cultural city really. Head to ‘Las Ramblas’ for half a mile of street entertainers, pet stalls, flower stalls, jewellry stalls and pickpockets. Most of them are immigrants from the Magreb, not meaning to be racist but keep your eyes open for them getting too close and if someone accidently bumps into you check your pockets. A trip to Camp Nou (Nucamp) is definitely a must - try to see a game if you can. They are all footie obsessed here so it’s just like being at home really. Go to the Olympic Stadium but do that first 'cause to be honest its tiny and a bit of a let down. Also the Magical Fountains (Font Magica) which on Friday and Saturday night, are all colourful and done to music. Spaniards don’t know how to drink. You never see anyone spilling out at the end of like night like Nexus 'cause they are all bloody sober! So us English birds have to show em how its done. So if you come to Barcelona expect a nice cultural time, don’t worry everyone speaks English but here are some phrses to keep you going anyway. A beer please - una cerveza por favor Egg and chips twice - dos platos de huevos y patatas fritas Piss off you Spanish twat - eres coño Español, vete a la mierda Your bird is a minger - tu tia es fea No, England are going to win the World Cup - no, Inglaterra va a ganar la copa del mundo Sharky"}, {"t": "USA Correspondent – Mike", "u": "world-usa.html", "d": "2002", "x": "After the Iron Lady and McGreggor closed the Sutton Manor pit in the early 90s I took flight to Germany with an American soldier girl based at Burtonwood. We were married in her home town of Lancaster Pennsylvania USA a year later which we visited soley for the marriage. I quickly discovered that the American choice of summer drink was 'unsweetened iced tea'. Having never tried this before and being told by my father in law that it was a wonderful drink, I gulped my first gob full and promtly spit it out on the side of his swimming pool. It was shite and I told him so. I added that we in England would never offer cold tea to our guests. We would pour it down the sink and make another pot. This ammused him no end. The only German language that I needed to know during my stay in the 'Fatherland' was the good old V sign, taught to me by Winston Churchill back in the 40s. Either that or the dick head sign as I drove around Germany in my car. Five years later we were posted to New Jersey USA where I learned the fine art of sea fishing from the Jersey Beaches and rental boats. I retired a year later when my wife finished her 20years in the Army and moved into Amish Country in Lancaster Pennsylvania and now we have a large house with a swimming pool in the back garden. I learned to play blue grass banjo whilst in the states. Four Amish villages in our vicinity are \"Bird in the Hand\" \"Paradise\" \"Blue Ball\" and get ready for it.. \"INTERCOURSE\"..The Film 'Witness' starring Harrison Ford was filmed in Intercourse. I am training to be a private pilot at Lancaster airport and enjoying every minute of the new challange.. When I lived in St Helens I was a piss artist of the first order but found a way out of the drinking life via a 12 step programme which I found in 1988. I was told on joining the programme that my life would change 'beyond my wildest dreams' and 14years later, still sober, I realize that my dreams are all coming true. I dont miss England but I dearly miss the folks around St helens and visit the town every year. I have friends and family living there and am in contact with them on a weekly basis via phone and computer. So thats about it. I am still a smoker but trying to stop.. see picture. Mike Grogan, Lancaster, Pennsylvania, USA"}, {"t": "New Zealand Correspondent – Geoff", "u": "world-nz.html", "d": "2002", "x": "Well first of all let me tell you that we are not alone we have a lot of other ‘telliners here but we only see them now and again.the firstthing that I found here was the fact that I could not make myself understood,the kiwis in the early days did not take too well to us Poms as soon as they heard our strong north of England accent they switched off and would not listen,I think they thought of us as thick terrace house dwelling,chip butty eating,bitter swilling ,idiots.I had the piss took out of me at work because of my accent,but I could give back better and they where so thick themselves they did not know I was taking the piss. Believe it or not we came across the age old scouse saying of woollybacks for us .I could not resist telling the scousers this’’you are living 12,000 miles away from home, in a land with 70 million sheep and you call us woolybacks’’. The cost of living was very cheap then as it is now but cars were very expensive back then for example in 1977 a 1967 Triumph 2000 would cost about $3,000 or 1700quid I was totally amazed at the shite that was on the roads. All this has changed now with the importation of used cars from Japan.This was all way back in the 70’s it all changed in the late 80’s and now we are accepted more as we now have people from ,hong kong,china,somalia.Taiwan for them to ridicule,New Zealand has come along way since we arrived it’s a lovely place to live and work ,but it would have been easy in the early days to give up and piss off back to ‘tellins,us ‘telliners can adapt and live anywhere and do anything,well almost anything . Geoff Lovett, Browns Bay, Auckland"}, {"t": "Sin Bin (pub & gig guide)", "u": "pubs.html#sin-bin", "d": "August 5th 2002", "x": "Former Applebys venue, decked out a la Liverpool wine bar. Real DJs who don't talk, actually mix. Despite the name, there are no references to rugby inside the bar at all. However, bog roll is extremely difficult to reach after having a shit"}, {"t": "Nexus Bar (pub & gig guide)", "u": "pubs.html#nexus-bar", "d": "August 5th 2002", "x": "Downstairs from the club of the same name. Equally-bad music policy, full of ripped bodybuilders in tight T shirts on the pull. Be careful not to spill someone's pint"}, {"t": "My Mate And The Gypsey At Sherdley (pub & gig guide)", "u": "pubs.html#my-mate-and-the-gypsey-at-sherdley", "d": "September 8th 2003", "x": "Well Me and me mate went to Sherdley show in 2002, and in the corner by the dirt ramps was a old tent. We decided to take a closer look....Inside was an old Gypsey woman covered in gold. She told my mate shed been expecting him. So i had to leave the tent....He came out and explained, \"Shes given me this letter, but i cannot open it for a whole year, Anyone else can read it but i am not allowed to see it or it will bring bad luck\"....So the next day he phones me up and says, \"Me Wifes Kicked Me Out\"....I asked why and he said, \"Well, i showed her the letter and explained she cannot tell me what it says...but read it..., so she read it and kicked me out.....\" He then went to his mothers and the same happaened there, his mother threw him out after reading this letter...shes practically disowned him. Hed had enough so he thought hes lay low for a year and keep the letter to himself until he was able to read it...... Hes Been at the local YMCA and has been pushin Big Issues outside woolies in town for a year.... Yesterday was his Final Day....so he thought....ill go somewhere REALLY safe to open this letter.....So he hired a boat and floated out into Car Mill Dam.... He Removed the letter from his top pocket......opened it........and then it blew off."}, {"t": "Charcoal Grill (pub & gig guide)", "u": "pubs.html#charcoal-grill", "d": "October 29th 2003", "x": "Everyone barr me has had a baptism in Steak Hellens it seems, but I used to keep quiet about my inadequacies and just nod politely when this local icon came up in conversation. Charcoal Grill, where have you been all my life! I loved it. Been to some classy places in my time and some right dives, but The Charcoal was something else. Having never been there, you see the tables and chairs as you walk towards it from the back of Wilkies, big sign saying entrance in the fan light over the door. All the while looking at the tables and chairs, the empty tables and chairs, you walk into the vestibule and try to open the door to the restaurant, it's closed, locked even. How were we supposed to know it was upstairs? Anyway we tramp the staircase past the bogs and up to the fella chuffing on a fag, who took our name. I mean sat there, in his parker smoking what appeared to be a cleaning ladies fag (Superkings I think) our Maitre d' was our first taste of what we were due to behold. In front of us were a gaggle of pensioners, who had tried to time it so that they just got in for the Earlybird menu, but because of traffic they had missed out. Gutted they were, but it just added to the spectacle. We walked into the bar. If your nans living room had been done out like Peasley Cross Labour by Lawrence LLewellyn-Bowen, this is what it would look like. We sat off and ate the crisps and peanuts and drank from our competitively charged glasses and chose our meals... well the menu, not fantastically wide in variation, sounded appealing. Aberdeen Angus steaks, with Au Poivre sauce (there is nothing quite as reassuring as someone correcting your French in a proper Telinz accent). We were shown to our table and within minutes our starters arrived. They came with salad and bread (cut diagonally with the crusts taken off, nice touch). I looked at the serving of butter on my side plate I could see the bread was dry, so I picked up a piece and started to butter, I felt my hand was slippy, something did not compute, it was like the butter was going straight through the bread and on to my hand. I turned the bread over. It had already been buttered and presented butter side down, just like me mam used to do. I could have openly cried there and then if I wasn't so up tight, beautiful. I dipped the double greased butty in my pepper pot and stuck it in my mouth before any of the wonderful staff noticed my faux Parr. The thing that made the waiting on staff extra special is that they were so nice, they never rushed you, weren't over every two minutes asking if everything is alright, they just let us have a good time and served and bussed our table with smiles and kind words. The steak itself was lovely, steak and chips as a meal just has to touch something pre-pagan within us all, we ate every morsel and felt good about it. The desert menu came back. I didn't know what an Apple Betty was before The Charcoal, but I do now, I'd recommend it to anyone to round off a meal. We then had a coffee to conclude, I decided on a liqueur version with brandy as a digestive, it came... wait for it... in a red wine glass! Attention to detail or what! We supped up, got the bill and left, happy and content with the start to the evening. We will certainly be back before long, they say that it is never as good as the first time and that you will always be searching for that first rush of euphoria; well if that's the case, it should be a load of fun searching. Everybody in Telinz has a right to go The Charcoal Grill and everyone should take the opportunity."}, {"t": "Gerard, The (pub & gig guide)", "u": "pubs.html#gerard-the", "d": "August 5th 2002", "x": "Long standing student favourite. Gothic type traditional pub with fascist landlord. Takes three years to get served because the bar staff always serve the locals first. Don't go during summer or any time when students are at home. Unless your name is Paul Calf - then you can go there to twat some posh bastards"}, {"t": "Bullion (pub & gig guide)", "u": "pubs.html#bullion", "d": "August 5th 2002", "x": "Dodgy underground pub with wooden panels and no obvious fire escape. Owner used to have a policy of only employing attractive barmaids with big tits. Sadly no longer the case. Singularly responsible for the popularity of Karaoke in the early 90s. Would be better suited as a seedy soho-type strip joint"}, {"t": "Forum 44 (pub & gig guide)", "u": "pubs.html#forum-44", "d": "August 5th 2002", "x": "Took over where the Nelson left off. Proof that NatWest Bank never turn branches into 'trendy' wine bars. Made famous by employing Warrior from Gladiators as a bouncer, before he got involved in drug dealing (or maybe not before)"}, {"t": "Dali Bar (pub & gig guide)", "u": "pubs.html#dali-bar", "d": "August 5th 2002", "x": "Now frequented by former Nelson regulars in their 30s/40s, singing Hey Baby, ooh aah, and pretending to enjoy themselves before getting back to the babysitter. Themed around Spanish surrealist painter, which means a few trips to Ikea for some predictable framed prints"}, {"t": "Java Bar (pub & gig guide)", "u": "pubs.html#java-bar", "d": "August 5th 2002", "x": "Up market student alternative to the Gerard. Polo neck jumpers, Gauloises, newspaper or book optional. Very generous host who gives away free beer. Can't complain about this bar for the above reason"}, {"t": "Aarf-Knacker ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#aarf-knacker", "d": "", "x": "Word used for large house brick. Good for 'lobbin' (see also L) at green'ouse winders - submitted by Jane W"}, {"t": "Ave ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#ave", "d": "", "x": "As in 'Its avin it down' - its raining heavily"}, {"t": "Barley ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#barley", "d": "", "x": "Apparently, a spoonerism of 'parley', meaning truce - used in kids games as an excuse for not being caught."}, {"t": "Bortered ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#bortered", "d": "", "x": "As in \"He was bortered in mud.\" or even clorped."}, {"t": "Bull Bitter ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#bull-bitter", "d": "", "x": "Half a bitter in a pint glass an a bottle of bulls eye brown ale. Why? Who knows?"}, {"t": "Burgie water ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#burgie-water", "d": "", "x": "The black liquid that came off them when it rained. It's been a bit of a saying for years for a bad pint...\"looks like fuckin' burgie water\"."}, {"t": "Chincoff ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#chincoff", "d": "", "x": "A \"Parrism\" from the 1950's. Meaning - a bad cold caught from various sources ie. sitting on cold doorsteps, drinking out of damp glasses etc."}, {"t": "Chinny ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#chinny", "d": "", "x": "As in being slightly annoyed or wound up by ones friend e.g.OOHH look at 'im, he's got chinny coz you et 'is pie!"}, {"t": "Clempt ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#clempt", "d": "", "x": "\"one o me favourite t'ellins words has to be clempt (possibly klempt) meaning starvin'... as in \"savers on yer pastie, ah'm clempt\"\""}, {"t": "Corporation Pop ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#corporation-pop", "d": "", "x": "Water"}, {"t": "Faffin' ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#faffin", "d": "", "x": "Messing, as in 'Stop faffin' about' contributed by Sean"}, {"t": "Father or favors ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#father-or-favors", "d": "", "x": "It means a person looks like someone else, e.g. Dosen't he favor Kevin Keegan...."}, {"t": "Fettled ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#fettled", "d": "", "x": "Fixed, sorted out"}, {"t": "Galoshers ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#galoshers", "d": "", "x": "Those black pump things that kids wear at school."}, {"t": "Geritetten ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#geritetten", "d": "", "x": "'Please finish your meal', possibly used in the context of 'Worart onobehtattall its brew tarm, lerrus gerris answashed and get snap tins and geritetten'."}, {"t": "Gerroff ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#gerroff", "d": "", "x": "Telling someone to get off ...or implying that there kidding you"}, {"t": "Grand National ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#grand-national", "d": "", "x": "Basically racing over everybody's hedges up the street - could be quite painful if you banged a knee on a hidden concrete post. Best played in Windleshaw Road."}, {"t": "Hanrags ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#hanrags", "d": "", "x": "Word of unclear meaning - sometimes used to call Saints when they were losing - more info needed"}, {"t": "Keks ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#keks", "d": "", "x": "Trousers - as used in the phrase 'the bastard spilt his pint all over me keks' - suggested by Big Ant"}, {"t": "Klempt ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#klempt", "d": "", "x": "\"one o me favourite t'ellins words has to be Klempt (possibly clempt) meaning starvin'... as in \"savers on yer pastie, ah'm clempt\"\""}, {"t": "Lobbin' ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#lobbin", "d": "", "x": "Word used instead of throwing. Not to be confused with 'lobby' (see L). - submitted by Jane W"}, {"t": "Lobby ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#lobby", "d": "", "x": "Hotpot without the crust. Ususally consisting of meat, (also substituted with mince if between Giros) potatoes, turnip & carrot. - Jane W"}, {"t": "Maud ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#maud", "d": "", "x": "Grilfriend - as in \"Gooin arrt wiff ar maud\""}, {"t": "Melt ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#melt", "d": "", "x": "As in 'Yer soft melt' contributed by Sean"}, {"t": "me - used grammatically incorrectly ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#me-used-grammatically-incorrectly", "d": "", "x": "Still in use today \"me\" at the end of a sentence. e.g. - \"ah proper fanceh an uxley's puddin me\". Or \"Aahm sick o' bein shagged rownd t'back o' Cindy's me. E sed e luvved meh.\""}, {"t": "Mither ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#mither", "d": "", "x": "(my-ther) - Fo be bothered by an idiot, eg \"STOP F*****G MITHERING\""}, {"t": "Moggie ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#moggie", "d": "", "x": "A mouse, definitely not a cat, apparently."}, {"t": "Nodders ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#nodders", "d": "", "x": "Condoms - used in the phrase 'lend us one of yer nodders'."}, {"t": "Owght ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#owght", "d": "", "x": "As in 'Any body want owght from't shop ?' - Anything"}, {"t": "Peas above sticks ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#peas-above-sticks", "d": "", "x": "You have ideas above your station"}, {"t": "Pilks - you weren't born at ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#pilks-you-werent-born-at", "d": "", "x": "You're blocking my view so get out of my way."}, {"t": "Put wood in th' ole ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#put-wood-in-th-ole", "d": "", "x": "Shut that door"}, {"t": "Quaarp ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#quaarp", "d": "", "x": "Rather than wasting energy using two syllables, 'Tellins folk turn the Co-operative Society's democratic nomenclature into a noise befitting a parrot"}, {"t": "Roaghm ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#roaghm", "d": "", "x": "As in 'Keep still, stop roaghmin' about' (shouldn't that be 'roaming' about, Ed)"}, {"t": "Sallywanger ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#sallywanger", "d": "", "x": "A word of unknown origin, used to scold a young child in days gone by,"}, {"t": "Samasase ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#samasase", "d": "", "x": "- 'like I said earlier', or 'like I say...' Word suggested by Mike"}, {"t": "Savus ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#savus", "d": "", "x": "To ask a friend to leave you something after they have finished with it e.g Savus on that tab, or savus on that butty."}, {"t": "Scon'yed ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#sconyed", "d": "", "x": "Scone Head, meaning 'fool'."}, {"t": "Singlet ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#singlet", "d": "", "x": "Meaning vest - i.e. underwear Submitted by Helen"}, {"t": "Skryking ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#skryking", "d": "", "x": "Crying as in - I`ll gi thee summat skryk abarht - submitted by BloorB"}, {"t": "Slutchy ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#slutchy", "d": "", "x": "Wet and very slippery mud which sticks to everything that comes into contact with it"}, {"t": "Snaped ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#snaped", "d": "", "x": "Unknown origin. Meaning - A bit upset about something."}, {"t": "Sniff - going on the ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#sniff-going-on-the", "d": "", "x": "Making ones focussed vocation to find a soul mate."}, {"t": "Snoo'in ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#snooin", "d": "", "x": "Or possibly 'snowing' - as in \"Snoo'in wi twat\", meaning \"the Plaza was full of nice girls last night\"."}, {"t": "Split ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#split", "d": "", "x": "Chips and Peas with anything i.e Split and Fish, Split and Gravy"}, {"t": "Stoney ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#stoney", "d": "", "x": "Alley way, back yard."}, {"t": "Summert ('Tellins Dictionary)", "u": "dictionary.html#summert", "d": "", "x": "Something"}];
